                    {
                        "form_id": "8c93f7d6-f901-4d69-9491-34c4c75d2963",
                        "entry_id": "1ec25890-c66f-3fda-a621-fd7ef23effa6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "подли́зах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "001b4e32-a4c5-3c76-9165-c88a1be4081e",
                        "entry_id": "1ec25890-c66f-3fda-a621-fd7ef23effa6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг., неодобр. угодливый, льстивый человек, старающийся добиться расположения вышестоящего"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77e7cb6f-0f49-4600-83fb-061d57af9e05",
                                "sense_id": "001b4e32-a4c5-3c76-9165-c88a1be4081e",
                                "text": "― Подхалимка чертова, преподавательская подлиза, ― шипела Лика вслед Вере."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc767029-3f51-4dea-a689-89085ee158c6",
                                "sense_id": "001b4e32-a4c5-3c76-9165-c88a1be4081e",
                                "text": "«Дрянь, а не человек! ― выражалась она резко. ― Подлиза! Втерся в мой дом, а затем скомпрометировал меня. Никогда он мне не был другом. Просто был собачкой на побегушках»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe25f2ca-e778-4cf3-a668-c7806d4b5b82",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ec25890-c66f-3fda-a621-fd7ef23effa6",
                        "source_sense_id": "001b4e32-a4c5-3c76-9165-c88a1be4081e",
                        "target_lang_word": "toady",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "toady",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                        "entry_id": "9ea4c4bc-4a75-384b-b910-737f1d542a2c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sycophant who flatters others to gain personal advantage, or an obsequious, servile lackey or minion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31a0d50b-763e-4d4a-affa-62becba9a532",
                                                "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                                "text": "\"Go on, Hiram, show 'em what you can do,\" urged Luke Fodick, who was a sort of toady to Hiram Shell, the school bully, if ever there was one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1713c21-8ed4-4630-8b8e-7f52fcaa23fe",
                                                "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                                "text": "\"But who is she, can you tell me?\" / \"Some fair-skinned speculation of old Montreville's, I suppose, that she has got either to toady herself, or take in some of her black friends with.—Is it possible you have never heard of old Mother Montreville?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40e82f43-428b-4171-a58f-9e6112567cdc",
                                                "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                                "text": "Before I had been standing at the window five minutes, they somehow conveyed to me that they were all toadies and humbugs, but that each of them pretended not to know that the others were toadies and humbugs: because the admission that he or she did know it, would have made him or her out to be a toady and a humbug."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ec58c94-8acc-4179-8de5-15d1a4d2b7f7",
                                                "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                                "text": "[T]he appearance of only three coaches, each drawn by four horses, was rather trying for poor Lady Scott. They contained Mrs Coutts – her future lord the Duke of St Albans – one of his Grace's sisters – a dame de compagnie (vulgarly styled a Toady)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7818964-c7b3-445b-9017-1d09d298f924",
                                                "sense_id": "decbe928-3b8b-3dd8-84e9-2884e329e9a6",
                                                "text": "But how could she have helped herself? I asked, imagining the sneers and the laughter, the adulation of the toadies, the scepticism of the professional poet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1986ef80-456e-3cc3-8d6e-d712d4882cde",
                                        "entry_id": "9ea4c4bc-4a75-384b-b910-737f1d542a2c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coarse, rustic woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "toady",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24fcba3a-9bf7-369a-8891-5b9ae8d53fbf",
                                        "entry_id": "e2cadf46-22eb-30e5-a937-21b7c2f7743e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave like a toady (toward someone)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61ce32d9-1175-40f8-b20a-5f28f36d2d68",
                                                "sense_id": "24fcba3a-9bf7-369a-8891-5b9ae8d53fbf",
                                                "text": "He had toadied to the late Mr William Morris: he had toadied to various members of the Fabian Society, he had toadied at first to the great Bransdon himself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "094f770a-07dc-36ca-b521-ba9410385208",
                                        "entry_id": "e2cadf46-22eb-30e5-a937-21b7c2f7743e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave like a toady toward (someone)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9fe82fa-dd7b-418f-b0f5-44707749037d",
                                                "sense_id": "094f770a-07dc-36ca-b521-ba9410385208",
                                                "text": "But bless your hearts, we \"ain't so green,\" though lots of us of all sorts toady you enough certainly, and try to make you think so."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "toady",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c8f8e63-1c2e-3c4c-a62f-51511b79bf75",
                                        "entry_id": "686d47d3-59a2-328f-a91f-38e401764db4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "toadlike"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1993f7d-bf6a-48d4-9a95-11172a5cdb72",
                                                "sense_id": "7c8f8e63-1c2e-3c4c-a62f-51511b79bf75",
                                                "text": "The bath is of greatest advantage in these chronic cases, with an earthy complexion and toady skin, if I am allowed thus to express its appearance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "toady",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "011d4ae3-3d72-390e-9447-d108790e4451",
                                        "entry_id": "635f6cae-7df9-393f-aafc-d679196a061e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Diminutive of toad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "childish",
                                            "diminutive",
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b8c13b27-94fb-4e63-87e1-f934698ce956",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ec25890-c66f-3fda-a621-fd7ef23effa6",
                        "source_sense_id": "001b4e32-a4c5-3c76-9165-c88a1be4081e",
                        "target_lang_word": "lickspittle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lickspittle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                        "entry_id": "9237ae7c-3f19-3971-904f-605b68da770a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fawning toady; a base sycophant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da80805d-2d36-4b4b-9502-749a0219035c",
                                                "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                                "text": "\"I've found you out and know you thoroughly, you mean, whining lickspittle!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac81f4f6-b181-4543-bde8-faeb83a2d08e",
                                                "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                                "text": "\"You're a suck, a suck and a lickspittle, that's what you are,\" said the pale man, his voice trembling with passion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c91ae6c-cc8d-48ac-b3d5-1d588adb3122",
                                                "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                                "text": "His preposterous insults were legendary, and there are accounts of his small-hour attacks on petty moralists and literary lickspittles in obscure Madrid dives where he chain-smoked and drank gallons of gin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6861548c-a545-4756-a2f0-ef3164bb2243",
                                                "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                                "text": "In Ottawa, Senator Marjory LeBreton claimed in a speech on Wednesday that allegations of spending abuses by her colleagues were “hyped-up media stories” that were inevitable in a “town populated by Liberal elites and their media lickspittles.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24db96fd-792e-4785-aefc-8f44f83dd4cd",
                                                "sense_id": "cd83de0e-e7f1-3efa-a4b7-33cc43d08ec1",
                                                "text": "“I frankly couldn't give a cat's knuckle about Gizmo. I mean, he's just kind of this fluttering lickspittle that is always bouncing about, always behind Nandor. But Nandor likes him.” “Oh, shut up, Colin Robinson. You're giving me the pip.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d0ed6c9-185c-3a34-a191-df5081fa5fae",
                                        "entry_id": "9237ae7c-3f19-3971-904f-605b68da770a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice of giving empty flattery for personal gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lickspittle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30ac5270-f353-357d-afad-8dea5c7664b3",
                                        "entry_id": "a5615e07-2724-3f66-ba27-f49629b2a6f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play the toady; take the role of a lickspittle to please (someone)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "706ac1b5-ca42-43fa-a6d3-f0100911e400",
                                                "sense_id": "30ac5270-f353-357d-afad-8dea5c7664b3",
                                                "text": "\"[Y]ou take his side, and that is wrong! ...If some young school teacher, or some young lad, lickspittles to him, it's bad enough.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
